<section id="S2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsection">2.2. Retrieval-augmented generation</h3>

<div id="S2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Retrieval-augmented language models combine external non-parametric memory
with a generator
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">19</a>, <a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a>, <a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>]</cite>.
Lexical and dense retrievers select candidates; late-interaction models and
cross-encoders refine ranking
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">38</a>, <a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">37</a>, <a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>, <a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">32</a>]</cite>.
Structure-aware variants use summaries, graphs, or hierarchies
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">39</a>, <a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>, <a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a>, <a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>, <a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">12</a>]</cite>.
Adaptive variants learn when to retrieve and assess evidence or answers
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">1</a>]</cite>.
Long-context and memory-QA studies emphasize evidence selection, granularity,
index keys, and temporal cues
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">25</a>, <a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">27</a>, <a href="#bib.bib50" title="" class="ltx_ref">50</a>, <a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>, <a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">15</a>, <a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">11</a>, <a href="#bib.bib43" title="" class="ltx_ref">43</a>]</cite>.
We use standard dense retrieval and reranking to assess what agentic
memory systems add to long-term conversation understanding.</p>
</div>
