all evaluation details are provided in Appendix <a href="#A1" title="Appendix A Experimental Settings and Complete Results ‣ Is Complex Agentic Memory Always Needed? Naive RAG Is Stronger Than We Thought" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A</span></a>.
<span id="S4.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Raw-RAG</span> achieves the highest score among the compared memory systems in six
of seven benchmark–model settings, excluding Full-context. It leads LoCoMo
by 0.65–0.95 points, LongMemEval by 0.13 points, GPT-4o-mini MEME by
2.24 points, and MemoryAgentBench by 4.48–5.53 points. MemMachine leads
DeepSeek-V4-Flash MEME among the memory systems by 1.52 points, while
Full-context leads <span id="S4.SS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Raw-RAG</span> by 19.98 points in that setting. <span id="S4.SS2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Raw-RAG</span>
is competitive across these tasks despite its simpler ingestion
procedure.</p>
</div>
</section>
