<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Experimental Settings and Complete Results</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We supplement the main-table comparisons with evaluations of <span id="A1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Raw-RAG</span>
under settings fully aligned with the corresponding prior studies.
Each comparison first specifies its evaluation setting and then presents
the corresponding results. Published baseline scores are retained, and
<span id="A1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Raw-RAG</span> results are measured in this study.
All scores use a 0–100 scale unless stated otherwise; “–” means
unavailable. Full-context uses no embeddings.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The remaining sections report retrieval and memory-management ablations,
context-budget controls, diagnostic analyses with uncertainty estimates,
and efficiency measurements.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsection">A.1. LoCoMo results</h3>

<section id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Evaluation and score averaging.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Raw-RAG</span>, judge accuracy is the mean of the binary correctness judgments
across questions and judge repetitions.
LoCoMo excludes category 5 and contains 1,540 questions: single-hop
(category 4; 841), multi-hop (category 1; 282), temporal (category 2; 321),
and open-domain (category 3; 96). The <span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Raw-RAG</span> configurations
use 256-token windows, 32-token overlap, 128 dense candidates, and 15 reranked
chunks expanded to complete turns.
Appendix <a href="#A7.SS3" title="G.3. LoCoMo LLM judge ‣ Appendix G Prompt Templates ‣ Is Complex Agentic Memory Always Needed? Naive RAG Is Stronger Than We Thought" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G.3</span></a> specifies the inherited judge
instructions, response parsing, failure scoring, and the limits of
retrospective format-failure accounting.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS1.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic ltx_title_subsubsection">A.1.1. Text-embedding-3-small setting</h4>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This setting uses text-embedding-3-small, with separate
GPT-4o-mini and GPT-4.1-mini reader blocks. <span id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Raw-RAG</span> uses Cohere
Rerank-v3.5 and follows the corresponding evaluation setting for history
access, answer generation, and scoring. Each fixed answer
receives three GPT-4o-mini judgments; category and overall accuracy are
question-weighted means of these binary judgments.
Table <a href="#A1.T10" title="Table 10 ‣ A.1.1. Text-embedding-3-small setting ‣ A.1. LoCoMo results ‣ Appendix A Experimental Settings and Complete Results ‣ Is Complex Agentic Memory Always Needed? Naive RAG Is Stronger Than We Thought" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> reports the matched comparison,
with published baseline scores from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dai et al. [5]</a></cite>,
our evaluations of SimpleMem <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">23</a>]</cite>,
and the MemMachine and Memora results from Table <a href="#S2.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ 2.2. Retrieval-augmented generation ‣ 2. Related Work ‣ Is Complex Agentic Memory Always Needed? Naive RAG Is Stronger Than We Thought" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.
SimpleMem, MemMachine, and GPT-4o-mini Memora are evaluated in this study;
GPT-4.1-mini Memora uses the published policy-retriever
result <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib53" title="" class="ltx_ref">53</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
