<section id="A1.SS1.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic ltx_title_subsubsection">A.1.2. Qwen3 retrieval setting</h4>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This setting uses Qwen3-Embedding-4B and Qwen3-Reranker-4B, with
GPT-4o-mini and GPT-4.1-mini reader blocks over all 1,540 questions.
<span id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Raw-RAG</span> follows the EverMemOS evaluation setting <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">10</a>]</cite>,
including history access, answer generation, grading
prompts, and score averaging. The judge is GPT-4o-mini-2024-07-18 at
temperature zero, called three times per fixed answer; accuracy is the
mean of the three question-weighted accuracies.
Table <a href="#A1.T11" title="Table 11 ‣ A.1.2. Qwen3 retrieval setting ‣ A.1. LoCoMo results ‣ Appendix A Experimental Settings and Complete Results ‣ Is Complex Agentic Memory Always Needed? Naive RAG Is Stronger Than We Thought" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a> presents the corresponding results,
with baseline scores from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hu et al. [10]</a></cite>.</p>
