<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate <span id="A1.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Raw-RAG</span> under the corresponding matched LongMemEval-S
settings with GPT-4.1-mini as the reader. The two full-set retrieval
settings use all 500 questions; the non-abstention setting uses the
470 answerable questions. Overall accuracy is question-weighted.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic ltx_title_subsubsection">A.2.1. Text-embedding-3-small setting</h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This setting uses text-embedding-3-small and includes all
500 questions, including abstention items. The category counts in
S-U./S-A./S-P./M-S./KU./TR. order are 70/56/30/133/78/133.
<span id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Raw-RAG</span> uses Cohere Rerank-v3.5 and follows the corresponding
history-access, answer-generation, evidence-budget, and scoring settings.
Each fixed answer receives three GPT-4o-mini judgments, averaged
over questions and repetitions.
Table <a href="#A1.T15" title="Table 15 ‣ A.2.1. Text-embedding-3-small setting ‣ A.2. LongMemEval-S results ‣ Appendix A Experimental Settings and Complete Results ‣ Is Complex Agentic Memory Always Needed? Naive RAG Is Stronger Than We Thought" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a> reports MemoryOS, A-MEM,
RecMem, Nemori, MemMachine, Memora, and <span id="A1.SS2.SSS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Raw-RAG</span> in this setting.
Published results are from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dai et al. [5]</a>, <a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">Nan et al. [30]</a>, <a href="#bib.bib53" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xia et al. [53]</a></cite>;
Memora uses its published policy retriever.
Full-context is omitted because it performs no embedding-based retrieval.
EMem and EMem-G belong to the 470-question setting in
Appendix <a href="#A1.SS2.SSS3" title="A.2.3. Non-abstention evaluation ‣ A.2. LongMemEval-S results ‣ Appendix A Experimental Settings and Complete Results ‣ Is Complex Agentic Memory Always Needed? Naive RAG Is Stronger Than We Thought" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2.3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
