<section id="A1.SS2.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic ltx_title_subsubsection">A.2.3. Non-abstention evaluation</h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This setting follows EMem and its graph variant
EMem-G <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib59" title="" class="ltx_ref">59</a>]</cite>: it contains 470 non-abstention questions,
with category counts 64/56/30/121/72/127 in the
S-U./S-A./S-P./M-S./KU./TR. order. It removes the 30 annotated
abstention items from the full set: six S-U., twelve M-S.,
six KU., and six TR. questions.
The <span id="A1.SS2.SSS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Raw-RAG</span> comparison uses the corresponding matched evaluation
conditions, including answer generation, judge prompts,
and three GPT-4o-mini judge repetitions.
The textemb3 configuration pairs text-embedding-3-small with Cohere
Rerank-v3.5; Qwen3 pairs Qwen3-Embedding-4B with Qwen3-Reranker-4B.
We reuse the existing GPT-4.1-mini answers and their three binary
GPT-4o-mini judgments, remove only the 30 annotated abstention items,
and recompute question-weighted accuracy. For the remaining question set
