<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsection">A.3. PersonaMem-v2 results</h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A1.T18" title="Table 18 ‣ Experimental configuration. ‣ A.3. PersonaMem-v2 results ‣ Appendix A Experimental Settings and Complete Results ‣ Is Complex Agentic Memory Always Needed? Naive RAG Is Stronger Than We Thought" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a> extends the evaluation to
PersonaMem-v2 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>]</cite>,
covering nine conversational scenarios. The <span id="A1.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Raw-RAG</span> run uses
GPT-4.1-mini as the answer model and is evaluated by multiple-choice
accuracy on 5,000 questions. We report scenario-level percentages;
its overall score is the question-weighted
accuracy.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Experimental configuration.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We fully align the evaluation design and retrieval backbones with the
EverMemOS comparison <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">10</a>]</cite>: the PersonaMem-v2 text
benchmark with 32k histories, the 5,000-question multiple-choice task,
GPT-4.1-mini as the reader, and exact-match answer-letter accuracy.
Specifically, <span id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Raw-RAG</span> uses Qwen3-Embedding-4B for dense retrieval and
Qwen3-Reranker-4B for reranking <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib56" title="" class="ltx_ref">56</a>]</cite>.
It indexes 256-token windows with
32-token overlap, retrieves 128 candidates, and selects the top 15
reranked windows, expanding them to complete source turns for the reader.
The reader uses temperature 0 and a maximum of 16,384 output tokens.
<span id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Raw-RAG</span> uses no persona profile; EverMemOS uses its profile-enabled
memory-management pipeline.
Appendix <a href="#A2.SS2" title="B.2. Query construction ‣ Appendix B Raw-RAG: Method Details ‣ Is Complex Agentic Memory Always Needed? Naive RAG Is Stronger Than We Thought" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a> specifies the retrieval query;
Appendix <a href="#A7.SS8" title="G.8. PersonaMem-v2 reader ‣ Appendix G Prompt Templates ‣ Is Complex Agentic Memory Always Needed? Naive RAG Is Stronger Than We Thought" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G.8</span></a> gives the exact reader input.</p>
</div>
