<section id="A1.SS4.SSS2.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Expansion overhead.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS2.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The mean lengths of the selected chunk bodies before display
expansion and headers are 3,734.9, 3,784.9, and 3,813.3 tokens,
on LoCoMo, LongMemEval, and MEME, respectively. The larger means in
Table <a href="#A1.T20" title="Table 20 ‣ Measurement scope. ‣ A.4.2. Evidence-length analysis ‣ A.4. Ablation studies ‣ Appendix A Experimental Settings and Complete Results ‣ Is Complex Agentic Memory Always Needed? Naive RAG Is Stronger Than We Thought" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a> reflect expansion and formatting
of those selected chunks.
MemoryAgentBench has a mean selected-body length of 3,550.5 tokens.
Evidence-assembly rules are defined in Appendix <a href="#A2" title="Appendix B Raw-RAG: Method Details ‣ Is Complex Agentic Memory Always Needed? Naive RAG Is Stronger Than We Thought" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS4.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic ltx_title_subsubsection">A.4.3. Cross-system budget control</h4>

<div id="A1.SS4.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This intervention freezes each system’s retrieved evidence and imposes a
5,000-token ceiling on formatted reader evidence, excluding the outer
prompt and question. It keeps a prefix of complete entries, with
token-prefix clipping only when the first entry alone is too long.
The full rule is defined in Appendix <a href="#A3.SS4" title="C.4. Context-budget interventions ‣ Appendix C Diagnostic Procedures and Statistical Methods ‣ Is Complex Agentic Memory Always Needed? Naive RAG Is Stronger Than We Thought" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.4</span></a>.
The reader receives at most 5,000 evidence tokens per question.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.SSS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The completed control covers six systems and all 14 sources
(2,071 questions per system). Mem0 and MemOS use earlier hosted-service
configurations, rather than their locally hosted counterparts in the main
comparison. Of 84 system–source conditions,
44 required new answers and evaluation after clipping; the remaining
40 reused their unchanged answers and judgments. The rerun reader is
GPT-4o-mini-2024-07-18 and the rerun judge is GPT-4o-2024-11-20
where the source metric uses an LLM judge; reused evaluations record
the GPT-4o alias. The historical clipping log records 5,545 changed
system–question contexts, including 1,479 first-entry cuts.
Scores follow the official weighting scheme: TTL averages the five-source
ICL macro with ReDial, and Overall averages the four capabilities.</p>
</div>
