<section id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Response parsing and scoring.</h5>

<div id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our judge requests use temperature zero without a JSON-only response
constraint. The parser first selects a brace-delimited object in the
first matching Markdown code block (with an optional json
language tag). If none is found, it selects the first non-nested
brace-delimited object containing a quoted label key and
string value, including when that object is embedded in explanatory
text. Otherwise, it attempts to parse the entire whitespace-trimmed
response as JSON. The selected text must decode to an object; the
label value is stripped of surrounding whitespace and
converted to uppercase, and only an exact CORRECT scores 1.
Explanatory text around a valid JSON label is accepted; bare
CORRECT or WRONG text is rejected.</p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">A WRONG label scores 0. Empty responses, malformed JSON,
missing or unusable labels, and other labels also score 0, as do
request exceptions that reach the evaluator. All outcomes remain in
the denominator with their assigned scores.
There is no format-repair retry at the evaluator level. Three
independent judgments are requested per fixed answer, and the reported
accuracy is their question-weighted mean,
