<section id="A7.SS9.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Evidence selection.</h5>

<div id="A7.SS9.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS9.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The judge receives a selected excerpt of the reader context. Selection
uses the ordered list of reference-answer values, ignores
values shorter than three characters, and finds the first
case-insensitive literal match of
each remaining value in the formatted context. Each match contributes
up to 900 characters before and after the matched span. Snippets are
concatenated in value-list order with […] separators, without
deduplication, and clipped to the 9,000-character limit. If no value
matches, the first 9,000 characters of context are used. The resulting
judgment measures the sufficiency of this excerpt for the reference answer.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS10" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsection">G.10. Result and path assessment</h3>

<div id="A7.SS10.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS10.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The task-aware assessment judges result and path coverage jointly.
It reassesses Tr in both phases and Del, Cas, and Abs after the update;
other task/phase rows keep the original semantic label. The
judge uses DeepSeek-V4-Flash, temperature zero, JSON-object
response format, and complete formatted contexts without a character
limit or the gold-localized excerpt above.</p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS10.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<div id="A7.SS10.p2.1" class="ltx_listing ltx_lstlisting ltx_listing"><div class="ltx_listing_data"><a href="data:text/plain;base64,WW91IGF1ZGl0IGNvbXBsZXRlIHJlYXNvbmluZy1jaGFpbiBldmlkZW5jZSBhbmQgcmV0dXJuIEpTT04gb25seS4=" download="">⬇</a></div>
